From 734a1d0e8b97853c7e6a964e877e154dc36e1c39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Denis Andreyev <257564291+unsound-mint@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:33:20 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Optional OpenMP parallelisation of the cost function

`make OPENMP=1` builds ROHSA with OpenMP; the default build is unchanged
(the directives are comments to a compiler without -fopenmp).

f_g_cube_fast now works one spectrum at a time (new routine data_term):
each Gaussian is evaluated once per channel and used for the model, the
residual and the three derivatives, so no residual cube is stored. The
parameters are read from beta and the gradient is written to g in place;
unravel_3D and ravel_3D only copied the same layout. The spectra run in
parallel. Each spectrum's share of f is stored, and the shares are added
in the serial order. The regularisation terms of f and of the b_params
gradient are summed per sky column and then over the columns in order.
The zero fill, the interior copy and the convolution loop of
convolution_2D_mirror run over columns in parallel.

Every sum has a fixed order, so an OpenMP build gives bit-for-bit the
same result as the serial build at any OMP_NUM_THREADS. Compared with the
serial code before this commit the result changes by rounding only: the
derivatives now use the exp() values of the model (gfortran vectorises
the model loop, and the vector exp() can differ from the scalar one in
the last bit), and the regularisation sum is grouped by column.
